From: RDK-B EasyMesh lab maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] orch: complete upstream command lifetime fixes

The 50-client carousel workload grows controller PSS from about 39 MiB to
673 MiB in three minutes and then loses placement ownership.  The active
queue can receive completed periodic commands faster than handle_timeout()
retires them because it destroys at most one command per pass.  Command
destruction is also not self-contained: direct delete paths omit deinit(),
and queue_destroy() frees borrowed em_t candidates unless the queue is first
drained.

Backport the remaining lifetime corrections from upstream commit
43f7f7127c8035ff18aa7a78eb82c1b22795ef1a (RDKBWIFI-498), adjusted for the
earlier lab fixes already in this series:

* retire every completed active command in a pass;
* make the command destructor own idempotent cleanup and drain borrowed
  candidate pointers before destroying their queue;
* make data-model cleanup idempotent and replace an existing cloned station
  object rather than orphaning it;
* release the TR-181 bus property after raw_data_set copies it.

The upstream change was LeakSanitizer-tested and held controller and agent
RSS flat for eight hours on a device.  Extend the existing station ownership
test so replacement and repeated deinitialization are exercised as well.

Upstream-Status: Backport [43f7f7127c8035ff18aa7a78eb82c1b22795ef1a]
---
 src/cmd/em_cmd.cpp                        | 10 +++++++++-
 src/ctrl/tr_181/wfa_data_model/tr_181.cpp |  3 +++
 src/dm/dm_easy_mesh.cpp                  | 13 ++++++++++++-
 src/orch/em_orch.cpp                     |  1 -
 tests/test_l1_dm_easy_mesh.cpp            |  6 ++++++
 5 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cmd/em_cmd.cpp b/src/cmd/em_cmd.cpp
--- a/src/cmd/em_cmd.cpp
+++ b/src/cmd/em_cmd.cpp
@@ -181,6 +181,11 @@ char *em_cmd_t::status_to_string(em_cmd_out_status_t status, char *str)
 void em_cmd_t::deinit()
 {
     if (m_em_candidates != nullptr) {
+        // Candidates are borrowed from em_mgr.  queue_destroy() frees any
+        // data pointers still held by the queue, so detach them first.
+        while (queue_count(m_em_candidates) != 0) {
+            queue_remove(m_em_candidates, queue_count(m_em_candidates) - 1);
+        }
         queue_destroy(m_em_candidates);
         m_em_candidates = nullptr;
     }
@@ -952,6 +957,9 @@ em_cmd_t::em_cmd_t()
 
 em_cmd_t::~em_cmd_t()
 {
-	free(m_evt);	
+    // Some event paths delete commands directly instead of going through
+    // em_orch_t::destroy_command().  deinit() is intentionally idempotent.
+    deinit();
+	free(m_evt);
 }
 
 
diff --git a/src/ctrl/tr_181/wfa_data_model/tr_181.cpp b/src/ctrl/tr_181/wfa_data_model/tr_181.cpp
--- a/src/ctrl/tr_181/wfa_data_model/tr_181.cpp
+++ b/src/ctrl/tr_181/wfa_data_model/tr_181.cpp
@@ -477,6 +477,9 @@ bus_error_t tr_181_t::raw_data_set(raw_data_t *p_data, bus_data_prop_t *property
     memcpy(p_data->raw_data.bytes, property, sizeof(bus_data_prop_t));
     p_data->raw_data_len = sizeof(bus_data_prop_t);
 
+    // Ownership moves with the copy; no caller uses the allocation afterward.
+    free(property);
+
     return bus_error_success;
 }
 
